The canonical restart limit already carries its transverse quadratic row,
gradient budget, coefficient-mass ceiling, and every continuous nonzero mild
row.  This module generates the corresponding `L²_t H⁻¹_x` forcing and feeds
the same objects into the domain-generic whole mild compiler.  The output is
the continuous representative of the existing strong whole-state limit.
-/

